    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθέσφᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>beyond even a god's power to
				express, unutterable</i>: or <i>not according to a god's
				utterance, unblest, portentous, awful</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμβρος, θάλασσα, νύξ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.273
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.373
			</span></i>; <i>vast</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. οἶνος, σῖτος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.244
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.211
				</span></i>
			; of great beauty, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕμνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					662
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρὴν ἱερὴ καὶ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					134.4
				</span></i>
			.—Once in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. θέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					232
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
